.TH LAUNCH-AI-WORKSPACE 1 "August 2026" "omni-term-ai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
launch-ai-workspace \- start the Omni Term AI tmux workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launch-ai-workspace
.RI [ session_name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates or attaches a dedicated tmux server (socket name
.BR omni-term-ai )
with a Command Center window and a Neovim Editor window.
Neovim is launched with
.B NVIM_APPNAME=omni-term-ai
so the packaged configuration does not replace
.IR ~/.config/nvim .
.PP
If
.B OMNI_JUMPBOX
is set, a launch with no session name SSHes to that host and starts the
workspace there. It does not mount the jumpbox itself.
.B OMNI_SKIP_JUMPBOX=1
keeps the session local.
A session name that starts with
.B @
is a host reached through the jumpbox:
.B sshfs
must succeed on the jumpbox or the launch aborts.
The target is one quoted argument, not a shell snippet.
.PP
The Command Center has three panes. The top-left and top-right panes each
launch a shell AI assistant ("harness") chosen with
.BR omni-config (1):
grok, agy, copilot, claude, codex, or deepseek.
The bottom pane is a plain terminal.
Harness names are shown in the pane's top border (tmux >= 3.2).
.PP
Prefix + Shift + W
.RB ( tmux
.BR bind-key
.BR W )
runs
.B omni-watch-row
on the current pane.
The pane's process stays in a 24-row rectangle and an 80-column pane opens beside it.
On attach, the launcher starts
.B omni-ceci-detect
once per session.
If a pane shows
.B /cecicela
and
.B --watch
on the same line, that detector opens the same row.
A
.B --work-dir
on that line is passed to
.BR ceci .
Set
.B OMNI_CECI_WORK_DIR
when the manual key should run
.B ceci status --watch
and the line did not name a directory.
.PP
If a chosen harness binary is missing,
.B launch-ai-workspace
prints the install command for that harness and exits non-zero before
creating any session. Harness API keys are read from the OS secret store
(see
.BR omni-secret (1))
and exported into the tmux session environment.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B omni-exec
Run a command with every harness API key
.RB ( XAI_API_KEY ,
.BR DEEPSEEK_API_KEY ,
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ,
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
.B GH_TOKEN ,
.BR GEMINI_API_KEY ,
.BR AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY )
injected from the OS secret store.
An empty stored secret is not exported, so an ambient token is left alone.
.PP
Fill-in-the-middle completion uses
.B OMNI_FIM_PROVIDER
.RB ( deepseek ,
.BR openai ,
or
.BR azure ;
default
.BR deepseek ).
Azure also needs
.B OMNI_AZURE_ENDPOINT
and
.B OMNI_AZURE_DEPLOYMENT ,
set with
.BR omni-config (1).
.TP
.B omni-secret
Store or retrieve API keys. Backends: Linux
.BR secret-tool (1),
macOS
.BR security (1),
.BR pass (1),
or mode-0600 files under
.IR ~/.config/omni-term-ai/secrets/ .
.TP
.B omni-config
Choose the harnesses for the top-left and top-right Command Center panes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/omni-term-ai/config
Selects the panes' harnesses:
.RS
OMNI_LEFT_HARNESS=agy
OMNI_RIGHT_HARNESS=grok
OMNI_JUMPBOX=
OMNI_FIM_ENGINE=native
OMNI_FIM_PROVIDER=deepseek
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMNI_TERM_AI_HOME
Override the share directory (normally
.IR PREFIX/share/omni-term-ai ).
.TP
.B NVIM_APPNAME
Set to
.B omni-term-ai
by the launcher.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omni-config (1),
.BR omni-secret (1),
.BR omni-exec (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR nvim (1)
